On 2004-10-19, Katy Johnson <kj2108nospam@barnard.edu> wrote:
> Is there an intrinsic to prevent being petrified by a cockatrice (or any 
> other petrifying monster)? I was under the impression there was not, and 
> I was playing a character that kept surviving "The cockatrice touches 
> you!" without stiffening.
>
> I am aware that eating acidic corpses stops the process, but what 
> prevents it? The only difference I could find between that and other 
> stoned-to-death characters was that I was wearing a mummy wrapping. By 
> covering the whole body, does the mummy wrapping make cockatrice touches 
> non-petrifying (like gloves & handling the corpses)?

No, wearing a mummy wrapping does not afford you any special protection
against stoning.  When a cockatrice hits you, there is a 1/3 chance
that you will hear its hissing [unless it is cancelled, in which case it
"coughs" and nothing else happens].  The hissing is what has a chance of
turning you to stone.  In general, there is then a 1/10 chance that this
will start you turning to stone.  The exception it is a new moon, and you
are not carrying  a lizard corpse in your main inventory, in which case,
you always start turning to stone.   Unless of course, you are polymorphed
into a monster which resists stoning, or a monster that polymorphs into
a stone golem when stoned (in which case you polymorph instead of turning
to stone).  Other than that, no there is no protection against it. 

Hope that clears things up..

